{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-outstep-day-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.66, step 7f. `scale-county-outstep-day`: CO and NOx at running exhaust, start exhaust and extended idle for the passenger car and the combination long-haul truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, January and July 2020, both day types, all 24 hours, `<aggregateBy key=\"Hour\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"24-Hour Day\"/>`, from the default database plus the time-aggregation county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, startsPerDay and the four hotelling tables). MOVESOutput is 8,752 rows, 2,188 per (month, day type), hourID NULL.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the 24-Hour Day output step: AggregationSQLGenerator groups each day type's 24 hour cells into one row (`yearID, monthID, dayID, null as hourID`) and, because the step `usesClassicalDay`, converts each to a classical day (convertDays, `x 1/noOfRealDays`) -- the division the output relation's cells already carry. The model emits it from `mos_*` with `n_outputSumsHours` 1; the slot's representative cell is the day type's FIRST hour, which is not the slot number, because `runspechourday` is hour-major (12, 15, 22, 25, ...).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 2188, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs per (county, month, cell), recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
